# MAAGAP — Docker build context exclusions
#
# The ML service image is built from the REPOSITORY ROOT, because data/ready/
# sits one level above ml-service/ and the service's path constants resolve it
# as REPO_ROOT/data/ready (see ml-service/Dockerfile's header). That makes the
# whole repository the build context, so everything the image does not need has
# to be excluded here or the daemon transfers gigabytes before the first
# instruction runs.
#
# The numbers are the argument: the working tree is ~4.9 GB, of which frontend/
# alone is 4.6 GB (node_modules and .next), ml-service/ is 177 MB and data/ is
# 58 MB. The image needs roughly 15 MB of that. Without this file every build
# would hand the daemon — or push to a remote builder — about three hundred
# times what it uses.
#
# ml-service/Dockerfile COPYs explicit paths rather than `COPY . .`, so nothing
# listed below could reach the image regardless. This file is about the
# context: build time, and not sending model snapshots and manuscript PDFs to a
# remote builder.

# -- VCS and tooling --------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.claude

# -- the frontend: deployed to Vercel, irrelevant to this image -------------
frontend
node_modules
**/node_modules

# -- data the service does not read -----------------------------------------
# Only data/ready/ is used at runtime, and only seven files from it (the
# Dockerfile names them). Everything else is pipeline input or intermediate:
#   raw/        the PPDO Excel workbooks and PAGASA PDFs as received
#   processed/  post-ingest, pre-feature-engineering intermediates
#   external/   PAGASA weather and PSA CPI reference pulls
#   synthetic/  generated fixtures
#   backups/    exactly what it says
data/raw
data/processed
data/external
data/synthetic
data/backups

# -- superseded model snapshots ---------------------------------------------
# Kept locally so a retrain's effect can be measured against what preceded it
# (D16, D21 and the weather/PSA/contractor-drop comparisons all depend on
# them). 132 MB across four snapshots that nothing at runtime opens, measured,
# and comparable to artifacts/ itself at 44 MB. These were also once
# committed by accident -- 32,630 lines in a single `git add -A` -- which is
# why the pattern is spelled out rather than relying on .gitignore.
ml-service/artifacts_pre_*

# -- training-only artifacts ------------------------------------------------
# The Dockerfile enumerates the artifacts it wants, so these are belt-and-braces
# for context size. The two regressors are 39.8 MB between them and are never
# loaded by the service -- they produce the MAE figure reported in Chapter 4.
ml-service/artifacts/*_regressor.joblib
ml-service/artifacts/oof_predictions_*.csv
ml-service/artifacts/*.png

# -- documentation and manuscript -------------------------------------------
second-brain
docs
*.md
*.docx
*.pdf

# -- tests ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not run inside the production image; CI runs them against the source tree.
tests
ml-service/tests
scripts

# -- local configuration ----------------------------------------------------
# Never bake secrets into an image. Configuration arrives as environment
# variables from the host's secret store, and common/settings.py's loader is
# written so that an already-set variable always wins over a .env file.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.log
